status: closed. >take. A calling names who answers, who does, who checks, and what is given first. No calling, no run. Face 04.

#03 >take compute answers alone only when the files decide
placed: 2026-10-17
issue: You asked whether compute can solve on its own. It can, but only where nothing needs judgment. If compute guesses, it becomes a pseudo-model (Sequence Addressing §17.9).
recommend: I think we should >take. Compute answers alone only when the files fully determine the answer. Two candidates, a missing piece, or a rule that needs reading means compute hands the question to the model, with what it found. It never picks.
path: `1009.calling/04.md`, The order of escalation
scale: 2
Ask: >take Compute answers alone only when the files decide. Otherwise it hands up.

reply: compute shouldn't guess, it should have a consist rules from which is completes all its work frome.  This will likely expand in time.  We will likely have forks in time that compute can choice based on exact specifications.  But if it's a miss it elevates to model then if that is a miss it goes to user.  That is our path.  First the compute using the desk to solve from the books it's holding, then it moves to the model to reason a path from a top list the compute hands so the model can pick outside of interupting the user.  Then the user is asked because all authority stops with them. if this aligns >take
status: closed. >take, with your refinement: compute works from consistent rules and chooses forks by exact specification; on a miss it hands the model a top list; on a model miss the user is asked; all authority stops with the user. Face 04, The path of a question.

